THOUGHT: NullAway reports overriddenInstanceStatus as @Nullable, so calling name() directly is unsafe. The method already handles the UNKNOWN status specially, but UNKNOWN is a valid enum constant, not null. To satisfy NullAway without changing behavior, I should guard the logging (and subsequent status update) with a null check, returning early if overriddenInstanceStatus is null. Then I must run the compile task to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/eureka && sed -i '401,409s/^/        /' eureka-core/src/main/java/com/netflix/eureka/registry/AbstractInstanceRegistry.java && sed -i '401i\        if (overriddenInstanceStatus == null) {
          logger.warn("Overridden instance status is null for instance {}", instanceInfo.getId());
          RENEW_NOT_FOUND.increment(isReplication);
          return false;
        }
' eureka-core/src/main/java/com/netflix/eureka/registry/AbstractInstanceRegistry.java && ./gradlew eureka-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

